<?xml version="1.0" ?><gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="GaiaGPS" version="1.1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd"><wpt lat="44.84172327800772" lon="-70.66097279017997"><time>2026-09-18T17:00:29Z</time><name>Night 1 Campsite</name><desc>Camped next to a big group of french canadiens teenagers, all boys. They had a cool satelite phone setup. We tented next to the lean-to.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="45.134919724494466" lon="-70.1712903344158"><time>2026-09-18T17:18:07Z</time><name>End/Car Parked</name><desc>Ended the trip around 8:30. So tired. Exhausting day. Legs in pain. Drove 5:30 hours home to Otis, MA. Got Mcdonalds on the way back. great trip.</desc><sym>car-24</sym></wpt><wpt lat="44.83690116481762" lon="-70.70998641759776"><time>2026-09-18T16:57:14Z</time><name>Shuttle Drop Off</name><desc>Where Greg Dropped us off. STart of our trip</desc><sym>bus</sym></wpt><wpt lat="45.12395688048588" lon="-70.34890364148657"><time>2026-09-18T17:16:11Z</time><name>Night 6</name><desc>Got a torrential downpour at night on my tent with the fly doors open. Got absolutely soaked. Heavy thunder all night long over us and the Bigelows.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="44.96994218707624" lon="-70.44542415066586"><time>2026-09-18T17:04:35Z</time><name>Campsite Night 3</name><desc>Hard ass day over Saddleback, the Horn, and Saddleback Junior. Junior kicked my ass. We were both tired. Poplar Ridge site is small and cramped. Lots of folks there already. Met &quot;Little Bear&quot; and &quot;Sans&quot;. Cool people. Met a few other passerby thru hikers. Nice tent bed we got. Rained at night and was pouring in the morning. lots of mosquitos. Ate Breakfast under the lean to while it poured outside before heading out.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="44.995671616706716" lon="-70.34165540843487"><time>2026-09-18T17:07:02Z</time><name>Night 4</name><desc>Spaulding lean to night. Bunch of old timers were in the lean to. Thru hikers all of them, but strangers. Tented here for the night. It rained a bit in the evening. Clear morning. Ate breakfast and chilled in the leant-to before hitting the road.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="44.90414933201117" lon="-70.52999903144163"><time>2026-09-18T17:02:42Z</time><name>Night 2 Campsite</name><desc>Tented here for the night. Huge campsite, lots of empty tent beds. Lean-to was nice, bathroom was super big nice and clean. Met a cool dude called &quot;Vermont&quot;, thru hiker, northbound. Loud group of women came in early in the morning at dark and stayed in the lean-to. They were from Boston.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="45.03179161657769" lon="-70.31322766482856"><time>2026-09-18T17:12:30Z</time><name>Sugarloaf Summit</name><desc>Cool summit. Tallest peak of the trip I think. Ski lifts and med station were there. and A heli pad. Had a snack here.</desc><sym>emoji-🗻</sym></wpt><wpt lat="45.03924002812798" lon="-70.342754940605"><time>2026-09-18T17:13:13Z</time><name>Night 5</name><desc>Camped by the river. Great spot.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="44.97287542263797" lon="-70.32633118260411"><time>2026-09-18T17:09:41Z</time><name>Mt. Abraham Summit</name><desc>Sick ass summit. Misty and slightly stormy, thunder in the distance. Low visibility, rocky exposed boulder field crest. Sickest summit of the trip in my opinion. WIndy at the top.</desc><sym>emoji-🗻</sym></wpt><rte><name>Rangeley to Flagstaff AT Section</name><desc>August 3-13 2026 Hike</desc><extensions><line xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/gpx_style/0/2"><color>E834EC</color></line></extensions><rtept lat="44.836925" lon="-70.709972"><ele>677.199219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836924" lon="-70.709969"><ele>677.199219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836911" lon="-70.709706"><ele>683.699219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836766" lon="-70.70955"><ele>687.699219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836641" lon="-70.709153"><ele>697.296875</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836704" lon="-70.709041"><ele>701.199219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836875" lon="-70.708898"><ele>707.199219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.836997" lon="-70.708762"><ele>712.898438</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837107" lon="-70.708606"><ele>719.199219</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837211" lon="-70.708413"><ele>725.0</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837377" lon="-70.708332"><ele>728.097656</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837717" lon="-70.708013"><ele>734.796875</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837695" lon="-70.707836"><ele>737.398438</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837748" lon="-70.707635"><ele>738.796875</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837873" lon="-70.707286"><ele>739.296875</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837911" lon="-70.70694"><ele>741.0</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.837995" lon="-70.706761"><ele>740.296875</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.838039" lon="-70.706525"><ele>740.097656</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.838124" lon="-70.706353"><ele>739.5</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.838436" lon="-70.705926"><ele>736.597656</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.838723" lon="-70.705527"><ele>732.0</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.839191" lon="-70.704993"><ele>724.296875</ele><time>2026-07-12T22:51:54Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="44.839368" lon="-70.70487"><ele>722.7